  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What holds",
      "items": [
        "The swap of PhoneServer.link is under a lock, and release() only clears the link it owns, so the old thread cannot drop phone B (wsserver.py 161–180).",
        "Phone A's page ignores code 4000 and does not reconnect (face.js 161).",
        "deliver() hands a frame to on_text only while its link is the current one, under the same lock as take_over (wsserver.py 161–180)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Fixed in 6b29b5a: the stale frame",
      "items": [
        "serve_ws checks link.open before it blocks in read_frame, so a frame the old phone sent before the close is still read (wsserver.py 283–286).",
        "Before the fix it went to on_text, which cannot tell links apart: a late imu or touch from A was published as B's, a late hello overwrote B's model.",
        "Now take_over and deliver share PhoneServer.lock: a frame being delivered finishes before the swap, and any frame read after it is dropped."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Evidence level",
      "items": [
        "Reproduced by test_the_old_phone_is_not_heard_after_a_takeover (test_wsserver.py): it fails on d2b04ac and passes on 6b29b5a.",
        "The contract check covers the takeover itself (a second MockPhone closes the first)."
      ]
    }
  ]
